.TH LEWITT-CLI 1 "October 2026" "openwitty 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openwitty-cli \- read-only diagnostic tool for the LEWITT CONNECT 2 (unofficial, experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openwitty-cli
.RB { devices | diagnose | list | probe " [" \-\-execute "] | read"
.IR what " [" options "] | \-\-version }"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B openwitty-cli
inspects LEWITT USB devices (vendor id 0x29c2) and performs single read-only control
transfers. It has no command that writes to the device. This software is not affiliated with
LEWITT, and its protocol knowledge has not been validated on real hardware.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B devices
List LEWITT devices from sysfs: descriptors, interfaces, bound kernel drivers and node
permissions. No USB traffic is sent.
.TP
.B diagnose
Like \fBdevices\fR, with an explanation of what each finding means for control access.
.TP
.B list
Quick libusb enumeration (vendor/product id only).
.TP
.BR probe " [" \-\-execute ]
Dry run (default) or execution of a small matrix of GET-only experiments.
.TP
.BR read " " api | version | status | settings
Read one message. Options:
.BR \-\-mock " (simulated device), " \-\-method " interface|device-recipient|detach,"
.BR \-\-request " uac2|uac1."
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 3 permission denied (EACCES); 4 interface busy (EBUSY); 5 stall (EPIPE); 6 timeout;
7 device absent; 8 unsupported; 9 bad response; 64 usage error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LEWITT_ALLOW_DISRUPTIVE
Must be set, in addition to \fB\-\-method detach\fR, to allow detaching the kernel audio driver
(this removes the sound card while it runs). Never set by default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openwitty (1),
/usr/share/doc/openwitty/USB_PERMISSIONS.md
